Testing & Verification
VLAN interfaces (Trusted/IoT/Lab) created, corrected, and confirmed up under Interfaces > Overview
Kea DHCPv4 subnets configured and bound to all three VLAN interfaces
Client-side VLAN isolation test (IoT unable to reach Trusted) pending physical switch and USB adapter delivery

Full log: docs/testing-log.md

Lessons Learned / Troubleshooting
Problem: Two of three VLANs were tagged on the WAN parent interface instead of LAN. Fix: Verified and corrected the parent interface for each VLAN under Interfaces > Devices > VLAN.
Problem: Kea DHCPv4 subnets were configured but not handing out leases. Fix: Kea requires interfaces to be explicitly bound under Settings, separate from defining subnet pools.

Full details: docs/testing-log.md

Roadmap
Wire physical switch and USB adapter; run real client VLAN isolation test
Pi-hole or Unbound for VLAN-aware DNS filtering
WireGuard VPN for remote access
Automated OPNsense config backups
Basic anomaly alerting (Discord/email)
